Version 0.8 (2026-11-25):
- Use libhostlist from flux-core. This removes limits on hosts per range
  (16K), string length (4K), and ranges in brackets (10K), and fixes many
  parsing and memory bugs. Invalid input no longer prints to stderr.
- Relicense under LGPL-3.0 to match flux-core.
- Support Lua 5.1 through 5.5.
- Fix hostlist.new() to use all arguments, not only the first.
- Fix hl:concat(hl), hl:delete(hl), and iterators after garbage collection.
  Iterators, map(), and expand() use a copy, so you can safely change a
  hostlist while iterating.
- Return integers from count() and find() in Lua 5.3 and later.
- Remove forced garbage collection, which made many operations slow.
- Install the module into a directory in the Lua search path (#5).
- hostlist: fix the --remove option.
- hostlist: add -L, --limit, --delimiter, --intersect to match flux hostlist.
- hostlist: deprecate -R, --remove and -f, --filter.
- hostlist: fix crash on empty input with -x, -m, or -R.
- Fix build with -Werror on glibc 2.42 and later.
- Convert tests from lunit to luaunit to fix a `make check` crash.

Version 0.7 (2025-08-27):
- More fixes for RHEL 9 and Lua 5.4 compatibility.

Version 0.6 (2025-03-07):
- Tag latest release for Lua 5.4 compatibility.

Version 0.5 (2013-12-20):
- Updates mostly for public release.

Version 0.4 (2012-10-03):
- Fix bug in hostlist find when prefix of hostname partially matches
  a prefix in the hostlist (e.g. hostlist --find=foo2 foo1-p2).

Version 0.3 (2012-02-16):
- Fix permissions on installed /usr/bin/hostlist.

Version 0.2 (2011-11-10):
- Fix bug in hostlist.union() that dropped final argument.
- Update to latest hostlist C code.
- Add hostlist -S, --sort

Version 0.1 (2010-01-25):
- Initial release
